// Movies: OpenMovie, DrawMovie, MovieWidth, MovieHeight, MoviePlaying and CloseMovie.
//
// FFmpeg's libraries (libavformat, libavcodec, libavutil and libswscale) are shared libraries, built under the LGPL
// next to the runtime (see dependencies.cmake), and are loaded when the first movie is opened. Nothing links to them, so a program
// that doesn't play movies doesn't need them and a program whose libraries are missing gets 0 from OpenMovie, which is what the
// original gives for a movie it can't play. They are looked for next to the program first, so a program is shipped with the libraries
// (blitzcc copies them there when the program plays movies), and in the places the system looks in after that.
//
// A movie plays by itself at its normal speed from the first time it is drawn (or asked about): the clock is the time that has
// passed, the picture that DrawMovie shows is the newest one whose time has come, and the sound is queued on an audio stream of its own
// a bit ahead of the clock. Everything is decoded on the thread of the program, when DrawMovie, MoviePlaying or Delay is called.
